1. Login to AWS console

2. Create EC2 instance: OS=ubuntu; Type=t2.micro; create new key; default VPC and Security Group

3. Launch instance

4. update security group inbound rules for SSH, HTTP, HTTPS, MySQL/Aurora(3306) from 0.0.0.0/0 (anywhere)

5. login to EC2 instance via SSH

6. Run following commands:
	- sudo apt update && apt upgrade -y
	- sudo apt install python3 python3-fastapi python3-pip apache2 mysql-server -y
	- pip install mysql-connector-python --break-system-packages

7. Run command:
	- sudo mysql_secure_installation
	[make sure you disable root remote login, remove anonymous users and test database]

8. update mysql config:
	- sudo nano /etc/mysql/mysql.conf.d/mysqld.cnf
	[update bind-address from 127.0.0.1 TO 0.0.0.0]
	Type: ctrl+o THEN ctrl+x

9. Run: sudo mysql -u root -p

10. Run: create user 'appdev'@'%' identified by 'Developer@123';

11. Run: grant all privileges on *.* to 'appdev'@'%' with grant option;

12. Run: flush privileges; Then Run: exit;

13. Run: sudo service mysql restart

14. check from local system terminal: mysql -u appdev -h IP-ADDR -p with password 'Developer@123'

15. Return to EC2 instance terminal

16. Run: 
	- sudo a2enmod proxy
	- sudo a2enmod proxy_http

17. Run: sudo nano /etc/apache2/sites-available/000-default.conf
	[add proxy details as follows:

	ProxyPreserveHost On
    ProxyPass / http://0.0.0.0:8080/
    ProxyPassReverse / http://0.0.0.0:8080/

	]

18. Run: sudo service apache2 restart

19. login to mysql:
	- mysql -u appdev -p
	- provide password as 'Developer@123'
	Run following SQL commnds:
	- create database student;
	- use student;
	- create table student_data(name varchar(20), course varchar(20));
	- insert into student_data('Prateek','Python');
	- commit;
	- exit;

20. Check from IP addrress using http://IPADDR, http://IPADDR/insert_gui, http://IPADDR/readall
